 "notes": "Seats are the 288 of the 2008 delimitation (ECI numbering, 1 Akkalkuwa ... 288 Jat). Districts are the 36 current districts under their current official names: Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar (formerly Aurangabad) and Dharashiv (formerly Osmanabad), formally renamed 16 September 2023 (Hindustan Times; Bombay HC upheld the renaming 9 May 2024); Ahilyanagar (formerly Ahmednagar), renaming approved by the state cabinet 13 March 2024 (the later central approval / gazette date was not verified here); Gondia (Wikipedia: Gondiya). Palghar was carved out of Thane on 1 August 2014 along taluka lines; seats 128-133 are Palghar. The only seat found to span two districts is Bhiwandi Rural 134 -> Thane (Bhiwandi taluka revenue circles, the bulk of it; the Wada revenue circle of Wada taluka is in Palghar). Vikramgad 129 (Vikramgad, Jawhar, Mokhada and part of Wada) lies wholly in Palghar. Other seats' extents were not checked one by one against the Delimitation Order; all other seats follow the Wikipedia list, which cross-checks with every district page that lists its segments. Regions: the six election regions used in seat tallies of Maharashtra assembly elections (Mumbai, Konkan incl. Thane, North Maharashtra, Western Maharashtra, Marathwada, Vidarbha). Ahilyanagar (Ahmednagar) is placed in Western Maharashtra, following the cited region tallies (Wikipedia 2014/2019/2024 election pages, The Telegraph 2014: Western 70, North 35); those totals only add up with Ahmednagar's 12 seats in Western Maharashtra (North = Nashik 15 + Dhule 5 + Nandurbar 4 + Jalgaon 11 = 35). Administratively it is in the Nashik division (North Maharashtra); moving it to MH_NORTH would give West 58 / North 47. Region seat counts: Mumbai 36 (Mumbai City 178-187, Mumbai Suburban 152-177), Konkan 39, North Maharashtra 35, Western Maharashtra 70, Marathwada 46, Vidarbha 62. Name spellings differing from the Wikipedia list (seat numbers are the key): Nawapur/Navapur 4, Chikhli/Chikhali 23, Arjuni Morgaon/Arjuni-Morgaon 63, Brahmapuri/Bramhapuri 73, Chandvad/Chandwad 118, Nalasopara/Nallasopara 132, Kandivali East/Kandivli East 160, Ahmadpur/Ahmedpur 236, Sangole/Sangola 253.",
